Description: QObject: only re-register timers the object still owns after moveToThread()
 QObject::moveToThread() unregisters the object's active timers from the old
 thread's dispatcher and queues a functor that re-registers them in the target
 thread. If killTimer() is called for one of those timers inside the migration
 window (after QEvent::ThreadChange, before the queued functor runs), the
 functor used to re-register it unconditionally. The object no longer tracks
 that timer (its id was removed from runningTimers and returned to the pool),
 so the registration becomes orphaned: ~QObjectPrivate() sees an empty
 runningTimers list and skips unregisterTimers(), leaving a {timerId, freed
 object} entry in the dispatcher. When the timer fires, the event is delivered
 to the freed object and the process crashes (use-after-free, QTBUG-151772).
 .
 Fix: the queued functor now checks the object's runningTimers list before
 re-registering each timer and skips ids the object no longer owns, so a
 timer stopped inside the migration window stays stopped. Also guard against
 a null dispatcher (moveToThread(nullptr)).
 .
 Requires the timer id serial fix (QTBUG-124496, upstream commit 21e9875d,
 packaged as QFreeList-return-timer-IDs-with-the-serial-included.patch):
 without it, a timer restarted inside the window could reuse the freed id
 and be wrongly re-registered by the stale functor.
Author: deepin
Origin: deepin, https://qt-project.atlassian.net/browse/QTBUG-151772
Last-Update: 2026-10-23
---
--- qt6-base.orig/src/corelib/kernel/qobject.cpp
+++ qt6-base/src/corelib/kernel/qobject.cpp
@@ -1432,11 +1432,22 @@
                 Q_ASSERT_X(res, Q_FUNC_INFO,
                            "QAbstractEventDispatcher::unregisterTimers() returned false,"
                            " but there are timers associated with this object.");
-                auto reRegisterTimers = [this, timers = std::move(timers)]() {
+                auto reRegisterTimers = [this, d, timers = std::move(timers)]() {
                     QAbstractEventDispatcher *eventDispatcher =
-                            d_func()->threadData.loadRelaxed()->eventDispatcher.loadRelaxed();
-                    for (const auto &ti : timers)
+                            d->threadData.loadRelaxed()->eventDispatcher.loadRelaxed();
+                    if (!eventDispatcher)
+                        return;
+                    for (const auto &ti : timers) {
+                        // The timer may have been stopped (killTimer()) while this
+                        // functor was queued in the migration window. Only
+                        // re-register timers the object still owns; a stopped
+                        // timer must stay stopped.
+                        if (!d->extraData
+                            || !d->extraData->runningTimers.contains(ti.timerId)) {
+                            continue;
+                        }
                         eventDispatcher->registerTimer(ti.timerId, ti.interval, ti.timerType, this);
+                    }
                 };
                 QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, std::move(reRegisterTimers), Qt::QueuedConnection);
             }
